---
source: tests/help_snapshots.rs
---
Print the coverage of each instrumented location of a run: whether the run
reached it, and the moment where it first did. Use it to find code that the run
never reached. Runs created before release 67.6 have no coverage.

`runs coverage` is an unstable feature: its flags and output can change in any
release. Enable it with `SNOUTY_UNSTABLE_FEATURES=coverage`.

Each location prints as one JSON object on its own line, by module, then
address. It has the `module_id`, `address` and `function` of the location, and,
when they are known, its `class`, `file`, `begin_line`, `begin_column`,
`end_line` and `end_column`. A location that the run reached also has
`first_reached`: the `moment` where the run first reached it, with its
`input_hash` and `vtime`, and `run_seconds`, the seconds from the start of the
test. The vtime is a JSON number. Several locations can start at one place, such
as the copies of a generic function, or the two outcomes of a branch.

Use --module to show only a module, by the ID that `runs modules` lists. Give it
more than once for more modules. To count or group the locations, such as by
file or function, filter the output, for example with `jq`.

While the run is in progress, the output is the coverage up to now. The run must
be ready or complete. If it is not, the command waits until it is ready, and
says that it waits.

Examples:
  snouty runs coverage <run_id>
  snouty runs coverage <run_id> --module <module_id>

Usage: snouty runs coverage [OPTIONS] <RUN_ID>

Arguments:
  <RUN_ID>
          Run ID

Options:
      --module <MODULE_ID>
          Only the module with this ID (repeatable)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Print NDJSON: one JSON object per line

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
